###  https://digicities.info/ontology#Flow
dici_onto:Flow rdf:type owl:Class ;
               rdfs:subClassOf dici_onto:Component ;
               rdfs:comment "Represents the movement or transfer of energy, materials, or information between components"@en ;
               rdfs:label "Flow" ;
               dici_onto:definition "A flow captures the dynamic transfer of entities (energy carriers, materials, etc.) between system components, including quantity, direction, and temporal characteristics"@en ;
               skos:altLabel "Transfer"@en ,
                             "Stream"@en ;
               skos:example "Electricity flow from the grid to a building; heat flow from a plant into a district network"@en ;
               skos:scopeNote "A Flow connects a source Component to a destination Component (hasSource / hasDestination) and carries a Resource or EnergyCarrier (carriesResource). Use the typed subclasses (ElectricityFlow, HeatFlow, ...) where one fits."@en .


###  https://digicities.info/ontology#FlowAttribute
